# cpan-board14 ROW-LEVEL FAILURES — the blessed baseline (task #1502, s473w,
# 2026-09-09).  One line per FAILING assertion of the 14-dist CPAN board, plus
# one synthetic `*FILE*` row per t-file that produced NO TAP at all.
#
# Columns: dist, t-file, test-number, description, got, expected, CAUSE.
# Join key: (dist, t-file, description) — NEVER the number, which drifts
# whenever PCL's row count diverges from perl's.  An unnamed row carries the
# empty description and #1041's rule then makes one key stand for all of a
# file's unnamed rows (Text-Balanced 05_extmul.t is 14 such rows).
#
# WRITTEN BY:  tools/cpan-scoreboard.pl --rows  (six columns)
# CAUSES ADDED BY HAND, and they leave BY EDIT — never by re-blessing a run.
# COMPARE WITH:  tools/cpan-scoreboard.pl --diff <this file> <a fresh --rows>
#                  [--board-baseline baselines/cpan-board14-s473w.tsv
#                   --board-current <a fresh --tsv>]
#                which prints NEW / FIXED / LOST and the CAUSES line, and exits
#                nonzero on NEW or LOST — the sweep's contract exactly.
#
# THE COMMAND (the `--no-dist-lib` applies to every dist AFTER it; oracle rule
# 2: Scalar-List-Utils' unbuilt XS lib/ must not shadow PCL's shim):
#
#   tools/cpan-scoreboard.pl --jobs 4 --timeout 120 \
#     --tsv baselines/cpan-board14-s473w.tsv --rows <out>.rows.tsv \
#     ~/.cpan/build/{Algorithm-Diff-1.201-0,Capture-Tiny-0.50-0,\
#       Class-Inspector-1.36-0,Class-Method-Modifiers-2.15-0,Data-Dump-1.25-0,\
#       File-Which-1.27-0,Mojo-DOM58-3.002-0,Role-Tiny-2.002004-0,\
#       Safe-Isa-1.000010-0,Sort-Versions-1.62-0,Sub-Uplevel-0.2800-0,\
#       Text-Balanced-2.07-0,Try-Tiny-0.32-0} \
#     --no-dist-lib ~/.cpan/build/Scalar-List-Utils-1.70-0
#
# REAL PERL WAS RUN BESIDE EVERY FILE (oracle rule 1), 183 of 183, with the
# same @INC rule and CWD = the dist root.  Seven files real perl SKIPS too —
# they carry the cause `PERL-SKIP` and are NOT PCL failures:
#   Class-Inspector class_inspector__devel_hide.t   (needs Devel::Hide)
#   Text-Balanced 94_changes / 95_critic / 96_pmv / 97_pod / 98_pod_coverage
#                                                   ("Author testing only")
#   Try-Tiny global_destruction_load.t              (needs Capture::Tiny 0.12)
# The scoreboard still calls them FAIL (its rule is "zero ok"); the cause
# column is what stops them being counted as PCL's — deliberately, because
# changing the verdict would silently rewrite four earlier snapshots.
#
# ONE MEASUREMENT THE CAUSES DEPEND ON, recorded so it is not re-derived:
# `tools/run-dist-t.pl` does NOT chdir to the dist root while the perl oracle
# does, so a test using RELATIVE paths fails for a reason that is not PCL's
# (measured on File-Which: 13/6 as the board runs it, 15/4 with CWD = the dist,
# 19/0 under perl).  Task #1575; not fixed here because it is a RUNNER change
# and would move verdicts under the snapshot this file is blessed against.
#
# THE POPULATION IS baselines/cpan-board-dists.tsv (s515c, #2950) and the
# command is `tools/cpan-board.sh TREE OUTPREFIX` (it reads that list; the
# `--no-dist-lib` dists are passed last).  The file keeps its board14 NAME
# because the tooling and the docs point at it.
#
# RE-HYGIENE s515c (#2950, the #223 recipe; 2026-10-11): main's code 973bdb1d
# measured (the shared base result base/973bdb1d for 13 dists + Scalar-List-
# Utils alone with --no-dist-lib) read 5 NEW / 46 FIXED against this file.
# The scratch board.sh had been running Scalar-List-Utils WITHOUT
# --no-dist-lib since s513 (38 files, 0 rows: the XS lib/ shadows the shim) --
# that alone was 36 NEW / 15 FIXED of the s513g "40 NEW / 74 FIXED".
# LEFT BY EDIT (46 keys) -- each with the window the shared base results or
# the session log place it in (not bisected further):
#   Capture-Tiny 13/14/15/20/21/22/23/24 "* is tied" (10 keys): s514d, tie on a
#     FILEHANDLE (#2590) -- absent between base d8936ef7 and 8f2fa11c.
#   Class-Inspector class_inspector.t "->subclasses ... evil ->isa": s514f
#     (#3140) -- absent between 52a8e706 and 973bdb1d.
#   Class-Inspector inc_to_local.t "Found ourself"; Data-Dump dd.t *FILE*,
#     dump.t/ref.t/regexp.t/scalar-obj.t/scalar.t/tied.t (unnamed); Sub-Uplevel
#     04/05 caller-override rows (4 keys); Scalar-List-Utils head-tail.t,
#     lln.t Tied, openhan.t (5), prototype.t @, reduce.t, refaddr.t (6),
#     reftype.t REF ref, scalarutil-proto.t (6), weak.t "$y is weak": fixed
#     between this file's s474 bless and s514 (absent from every s514 base);
#     the session log names the families: openhandle s500a/s510f, set_prototype
#     s502e, refaddr s508a, weaken/looks_like_number on a tie s492a, reftype
#     s495f, Data::Dump s495f/s499j/s514a.
# ENTERED BY HAND (5 rows): Data-Dump quote.t #12 (#2066), Role-Tiny
# role-basic-composition.t "role method applied" (#3001), Try-Tiny finally.t
# 10-12 (the dist's own Try::Tiny since s499j: DESTROY at scope exit, #2370).
